From: nuno407 <11352538+nuno407@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:03:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/45] wifi: mwifiex: use the legacy scan with pre-14.68
 firmware

The 88W8797 firmware with Bluetooth on UART (14.62.17.p215), which the
Surface RT needs for Bluetooth, rejects HostCmd_CMD_802_11_SCAN_EXT with
result 2, so the interface never finds a network. Use the legacy scan
command when the firmware is older than 14.68.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cmdevt.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cmdevt.c b/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cmdevt.c
index 29e0f2745..eac2c8cea 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cmdevt.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cmdevt.c
@@ -1530,6 +1530,16 @@ int mwifiex_ret_get_hw_spec(struct mwifiex_private *priv,
 
 	adapter->fw_release_number = le32_to_cpu(hw_spec->fw_release_number);
 	adapter->fw_api_ver = (adapter->fw_release_number >> 16) & 0xff;
+	/*
+	 * The 88W8797 firmware with Bluetooth on UART (14.62.17.p215, as used on the
+	 * Microsoft Surface RT) rejects the extended scan command
+	 * (0x107, result 2); 14.68 firmware takes it. Fall back to the legacy scan command.
+	 */
+	if (adapter->ext_scan && adapter->fw_api_ver == 14 &&
+	    ((adapter->fw_release_number >> 8) & 0xff) < 68) {
+		mwifiex_dbg(adapter, MSG, "firmware has no extended scan, using legacy scan\n");
+		adapter->ext_scan = false;
+	}
 	adapter->number_of_antenna =
 			le16_to_cpu(hw_spec->number_of_antenna) & 0xf;
 
